{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CecGUQhonoRhtJN34VGSE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All tests pass. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Summary\n\nThe test suite was failing because POSIX character class patterns (like `[[:alnum:]]`) were not being properly handled in gitignore patterns. \n\n**Changes made to `/tmp/tb3-run-KsUuoI/repo/pathspec/patterns/gitignore/base.py`:**\n\n1. **Added POSIX class mappings** - Defined a dictionary mapping valid POSIX class names to their ASCII-equivalent regex patterns (e.g., `[:alnum:]` → `[0-9A-Za-z]`)\n\n2. **Fixed bracket expression parsing** - Modified the algorithm that finds the closing bracket of a bracket expression to skip over POSIX class patterns like `[:...:]]`, so it doesn't stop at the first `]` (which closes the POSIX class) but continues to find the actual bracket expression closing bracket.\n\n3. **Implemented POSIX class detection and translation** - After parsing the bracket content, check if it's a valid POSIX class pattern. If valid, translate it to the ASCII equivalent. If invalid (like `[[:Alpha:]]` with uppercase or `[[:bogus:]]` with an unknown class name), discard the pattern by raising a `_RangeError`, which causes Git to treat it as malformed.\n\n**Test results:** ✅ All 200 tests passing (276 skipped as before)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1173,"cache_read_input_tokens":99524,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1173},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"54e9d7c1-1345-5e2d-ba67-93201e1134e8","uuid":"5e66cbd4-5c32-4bc1-bb3a-fde128fcc1bf","timestamp":"2026-09-01T06:44:46.527Z","request_id":"req_011CecGUPdZo4ZLjVwok2fW1"}
